#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""퇴근 hand-over, phase 1 of api#1049 (요유 2026-11-06): the main pane stays on the 회사맥, and its panes on the workers server
carry on on 집맥 while the 회사맥 sleeps.

    workers-move go             start the move in the background and return; its summary reaches the main pane by pane-tell
    workers-move list           the panes go would ask, changing nothing
    workers-move bridge         workers-watch runs it every minute on the 회사맥: what moved panes said on 집맥 reaches the main pane
    workers-move tell <pane> <text>   type into a moved pane on 집맥 (pane-tell there, over ssh)
    workers-move read <pane>    that pane's screen
    workers-move resume         tell each pane go left on the 회사맥 to carry on (after 출근)
    workers-move --selftest

A move, per pane of the main pane on workers (agent name spawn-<main terminal>-, never a check pane or another lead's):
1. `{state}/orchestrator/moving/<terminal>` is made, so auto-tab-close sends that pane's next reply nowhere, and the pane is
   asked to stop after its current tool call, commit WIP on its branch, stop watching Slack threads, and reply with a handoff
   note that starts `[인계 메모] 옮김` or `[인계 메모] 옮기지 않음: <why>` and names its `폴더:`. A pane at a question dialog
   is not asked: typed text would answer the dialog.
2. Once the note is its last reply, the folder is checked: a git folder must be clean, on a branch, and either a linked
   worktree on a feature branch (pushed here: a Codex pane has no network) or the default branch with nothing unpushed. No
   commit is ever made here: a shared checkout may hold another session's files.
3. 집맥 (ssh to ~/.config/herdr/remote-host): the same path is made ready (a worktree from that Mac's clone of the repo, or the
   existing checkout fast-forwarded), the note and the pane's first instruction are written to
   ~/.local/state/workers-move/memos/<agent>.md there, and `pane-spawn --opener <main terminal>` opens a pane on 집맥's workers
   server that reads it (Codex, else Claude when Codex stops at a trust dialog).
4. Only then is the 회사맥 pane marked reported and closed: a 집맥 pane that did not open leaves the 회사맥 pane as it was.
A pane that will not move stays, is marked reported (its note was its report), and `resume` tells it to go on. Each step is
saved in moves.json, so a run cut by sleep goes on where it was. A run that died while opening a 집맥 pane, or an ssh call that
broke during the open, leaves step `unknown`: never a second 집맥 pane, and never a resume of the same work here. One run at a
time (run.lock).

The bridge reads, over one ssh call, 집맥's workers pane list and the new part of its pane report day files. Entries of moved
panes (auto-tab-close's reports, workers-watch's `[workers-watch]` alerts) are copied into this Mac's day file under the address
`집맥:workers/<pane>`, so every reader of `전체 보고: <file> (<time> 항목)` finds them, and queued; each goes to the main pane in
order, a report through auto-tab-close's route_main_report, so a finished one gets its check pane as any other. Before that the
회사맥 folder is fast-forwarded to the branch, since the check runs here; if it cannot be, the report goes straight through with
the reason. What did not go stays queued for the next minute. A move ends once its 집맥 pane has been gone for a minute and
nothing of it waits.

Test env: WORKERS_MOVE_SSH (a command in place of ssh and its options), WORKERS_MOVE_REMOTE (ssh target), WORKERS_MOVE_TELL
(a pane-tell), WORKERS_MOVE_WAIT (seconds to wait for notes, 900), WORKERS_MOVE_POLL (5), WORKERS_MOVE_FG=1 (go runs in front).
On the remote side: WORKERS_MOVE_REMOTE_SPAWN (a pane-spawn), WORKERS_MOVE_REMOTE_PATH.
"""
